[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=DeepSeek Monitor
Comment=Start the DeepSeek monitor app (Tkinter "Cost & Usage")
Icon=/home/USER/DeepSeek-Monitor/assets/deepseek-monitor-256.png
Exec=sh -c 'exec python3 "$HOME/DeepSeek-Monitor/deepseek_rates.py"'
Terminal=false
Categories=Development;Network;
Keywords=DeepSeek;Monitor;Cost;Usage;Tkinter;

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example desktop entry to start the monitor app (Tkinter GUI).
#
# How to use:
#   1. The `Exec=` line uses `sh -c` with `$HOME`, so it works on any machine
#      without editing — regardless of username. If you cloned the repo under
#      a different folder name, adjust `DeepSeek-Monitor` in the `Exec=` line.
#   2. The `Icon=` field is resolved by the desktop environment WITHOUT a
#      shell, so `$HOME` does not expand there. Replace `/home/USER` with your
#      absolute home path in the `Icon=` line, or install the icon to
#      ~/.local/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/deepseek-monitor.svg and
#      set `Icon=deepseek-monitor`.
#   3. The monitor app only needs the stdlib + tkinter, so a plain `python3`
#      is usually enough (no virtualenv required).
#   4. Copy this file to ~/.local/share/applications/deepseek-monitor.desktop
#      (or /usr/share/applications/ for all users).
#
# A desktop entry does NOT need the executable bit.
#
# The monitor is a GUI app (Terminal=false); it shows the tariff widget,
# the "Cost & Usage" window and the settings. It reads usage from the local
# proxy/SQLite or a central InfluxDB (see docs/INSTALLATION.md).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
